# Design System — Token-First

All visual tokens live in `src/utils/` (plus Three.js colors in `threeJSColors.ts`).

| Concern | File |
|---------|------|
| Space / size (pad, margin, gap, w/h) | `src/utils/goldenRatio.ts` |
| Type (size, tracking, weight, line-height) | `src/utils/typo.ts` |
| UI colors (exact names: `ColorBlack`…) | `src/utils/color.ts` |
| Three.js / shader colors | `src/components/threejs/threeJSColors.ts` |

## When the user gives something new

1. **New font / type value** (family, size, tracking, weight, line-height) → **update `typo.ts` first** (and font load in `typo.scss` / layout if family changes), then wire components to the new token.
2. **New UI color** (hex / name) → **update `color.ts` first** (exact `Color*` name), then wire components. Also refresh `colorCssVars` if used globally.
3. **New Three.js color** → **update `threeJSColors.ts` first**, then controls / shaders.
4. **New spacing size** → match / add via `goldenRatio.ts` (`Scale*`), then use it.

Never hardcode a new font or color only in a component. Token file → then usage.
